The Dart log is too compact to show every file, so I also ran the two new Dart test files directly: all 19 pass.

**Things you should know**
- **Browser build fix outside the brief's files.** Adding the DHT to the REPL broke the browser `demo` build, through two Node-only modules: `node:crypto` and `dgram`. I changed both to load when first used, the same approach `yin.repl.store` already uses for `fs`. The files are `dao.jing.dht` (S4) and `dao.stream.datagram.node` (S1). `demo` and `yin-repl` now both build.
- **One failure I can't fully explain.** One full JVM run failed 3 assertions in the Dart-client test in `main-test`, using a Dart peer binary built before the restructure. After I rebuilt the binary, that test and the full lane both passed. It was either the stale binary or a timing flake.
- **"No peers means solo" is read literally.** `--dht-port` or `--dht-bind` without a peer is refused, so a first node has to list its peers' addresses in advance.
- **`join {:dir …}` takes no directory lock.** The lock code lives in `yin.repl.store.fs`. The REPL passes its locked store instead; moving the lock under `dao.*` is an open decision.
- **Node leg needs a manual build.** The Node part of the process test needs `target/yin-repl.js`, which no bb task builds. When the file is absent the test skips that part and prints a notice.

